{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>If for the rod</b> — to destroy the seed." "<b>or for His land</b> — or for the rod, like: 'great stones and rain in the sea.' And behold, he mentioned three matters: the first for correction, the second for His land, because of the need of the land and its inhabitants, the devout, as in the matter of לפעלם. And the third for His kindness. And behold, it returns: 'whether for the rod, whether for His land,' meaning לפעלם."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {1 "The phrase 'אבנים גדולות וגשם בים' appears to cite a verse or proverb about hail and rain in the sea; left untranslated as the reference is not fully resolved. The repeated term לפעלם (a biblical Hebrew form meaning 'for their deed/need' or similar) is retained in Hebrew as Ibn Ezra uses it as a technical reference point."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:54.386043110Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}